# Generated from: specs/485-reject-non-issue-legacy-dependency-references-instead-of-aborting-upgrade-detection/requirements.md
Feature: Non-issue legacy dependency references do not abort upgrade detection

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: AC1 pull-request and table-row references create no candidate
    Given an issue body containing "| **Version / Commit** | Main after merged PR #307 |" and "requires the fix after PR #307"
    When parseLegacyDependencyEvidence parses the body
    Then it returns no edge for "#307"

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: AC2 references qualified with another project or repository create no candidate
    Given an issue body containing "PennyScan issue #102 therefore fails" and "depends on Other-Org/other-repo#12"
    When parseLegacyDependencyEvidence parses the body
    Then it returns no edge for "#102" or "#12"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: AC3 a dangling legacy candidate becomes a finding and detection completes
    Given a repository issue graph and a legacy candidate edge whose endpoint is not a repository issue
    When detectIssueDependencyUpgrade runs
    Then the candidate is absent from additions
    And findings contain it with reason "dependency_dangling_candidate" and its source line
    And the detect report contains every other detected category

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: AC4 genuine sequencing clauses and field lines are preserved
    Given issue bodies containing "After issue #394 resumes a consumed dispatch" and "Depends on: #10, #11"
    And #394, #10 and #11 are repository issues
    When detection runs
    Then the edges blockedBy #394, blockedBy #10 and blockedBy #11 are proposed

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: AC5 dangling existing official edges still fail closed
    Given an existing official blocked-by edge whose target is not readable as a repository issue
    When detection or sdlc-execute graph validation runs
    Then it reports "dependency_dangling"
